WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:03.280
Can an acclaimed actor's&nbsp;
death be news a decade later?&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:03.280 --> 00:00:08.194
Apparently so. Why don't people remember&nbsp;
that Michael Clarke Duncan passed away?

00:00:08.194 --> 00:00:12.400
Without any movie magic, Michael&nbsp;
Clarke Duncan was a giant.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:12.400 --> 00:00:16.800
According to Biography, he stood&nbsp;
6'5" and weighed over 300 pounds,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:20.640
which helped him pay the bills while he was&nbsp;
working to become an actor in Hollywood.

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:24.800
Before starring in movies, Duncan worked&nbsp;
as a bouncer and bodyguard for many notable&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:24.800 --> 00:00:30.240
stars of the 1990s, including Martin&nbsp;
Lawrence, LL Cool J, and Will Smith.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:30.240 --> 00:00:34.720
According to the Rockland County Times, Duncan&nbsp;
quit working as a bodyguard when another of his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:34.720 --> 00:00:40.640
clients, The Notorious B.I.G, was shot and&nbsp;
killed in 1997. When Duncan started acting,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:40.640 --> 00:00:43.760
he played tough-guy roles until&nbsp;
bigger roles came calling.

00:00:43.760 --> 00:00:47.360
"Ain't that right, Tiny?"
"Shut up."

00:00:47.360 --> 00:00:52.160
While Duncan's size proved helpful in starting&nbsp;
his career, the actor was conscious of his health.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:57.120
In an interview with CNN in 2006, Duncan&nbsp;
explained that he turned his life around&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:00:57.120 --> 00:01:01.360
following a visit with a doctor. He didn't go&nbsp;
into detail about what the doctor told him,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:01.360 --> 00:01:05.760
but he clearly learned his weight and health&nbsp;
were something he needed to take seriously.

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.087
"He said, 'Can I be honest with you?' and I said&nbsp;
'No.' I said, 'You don't have to say anything.'"

00:01:11.087 --> 00:01:16.240
By the late 2000s, Michael Clarke Duncan&nbsp;
seemed pretty healthy. He even appeared in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:16.240 --> 00:01:21.360
an advertising campaign for PETA, saying&nbsp;
he lost 35 pounds from a vegetarian diet.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:25.040
But his health wasn't especially&nbsp;
good for years before he started it.

00:01:25.040 --> 00:01:30.960
Duncan's health made headlines on July 13, 2012,&nbsp;
when he was admitted to the Intensive Care Unit&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:30.960 --> 00:01:36.480
at a Los Angeles hospital. According to TMZ, he&nbsp;
was found in cardiac arrest by his girlfriend,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:36.480 --> 00:01:40.480
Omarosa Manigault, at around&nbsp;
2:00 a.m. She performed CPR&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:40.480 --> 00:01:44.880
and managed to resuscitate Duncan, who was&nbsp;
transported to the hospital for treatment.

00:01:44.880 --> 00:01:49.760
"I just started praying. I mean, I&nbsp;
prayed like I have never prayed before."

00:01:49.760 --> 00:01:51.760
Duncan's publicist told TMZ,

00:01:51.760 --> 00:01:55.840
"According to doctors, Michael Clarke&nbsp;
Duncan suffered a myocardial infarction&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:55.840 --> 00:01:59.600
early this morning. He is now stable, and&nbsp;
we look forward to his full recovery."

00:01:59.600 --> 00:02:05.680
Duncan died on September 3, 2012, at the age&nbsp;
of 54. So there were several weeks in which,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.680 --> 00:02:10.560
as far as the public was concerned, Duncan was&nbsp;
on the mend. But Duncan continued to undergo&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:16.000
treatment because he hadn't fully recovered.&nbsp;
Shortly before he died, he lapsed into a coma. His&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:16.000 --> 00:02:21.055
publicist later explained that his cause of death&nbsp;
was from complications from his heart attack.

00:02:21.055 --> 00:02:27.360
At the time of his death, Duncan was dating&nbsp;
Omarosa Manigault, now Omarosa Manigault Newman,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:27.360 --> 00:02:32.000
best known as an "Apprentice" contestant and&nbsp;
later as a member of President Donald Trump's&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:32.000 --> 00:02:36.320
White House staff. Reports of family&nbsp;
infighting took over the narrative.

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:41.360
Duncan's family accused Manigault of manipulating&nbsp;
him in his final days. They further alleged&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.360 --> 00:02:45.680
she lied about their engagement and sold off&nbsp;
several of his belongings without permission.

00:02:45.680 --> 00:02:51.040
Omarosa's behavior threw up red flags for&nbsp;
Duncan's family, including Omarosa's questions&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:51.040 --> 00:02:55.600
about Duncan's will. Omarosa also wouldn't&nbsp;
allow Duncan's family to stay at his home,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:55.600 --> 00:02:59.840
even though they came in from out of town.&nbsp;
Duncan's niece claimed Omarosa likewise&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.840 --> 00:03:04.560
asked for or attempted to secure Duncan's&nbsp;
sperm while he was comatose. According to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.560 --> 00:03:09.573
The New York Daily News, the infighting&nbsp;
left Duncan's grave unmarked for a year.

00:03:09.573 --> 00:03:15.440
Michael Clarke Duncan worked steadily starting&nbsp;
with an uncredited role in "Friday" in 1995.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:15.440 --> 00:03:19.520
His big break came when he was&nbsp;
cast to play Bear in "Armageddon."&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:19.520 --> 00:03:24.720
From there, he truly blew up thanks to his&nbsp;
portrayal of John Coffey in "The Green Mile."

00:03:24.720 --> 00:03:27.600
He received an Academy Award&nbsp;
nomination for that performance,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:27.600 --> 00:03:32.720
among other award nominations and wins, so it's&nbsp;
often considered his most significant role.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:35.200
"I'm tired, boss."

00:03:35.920 --> 00:03:39.920
He followed this role with appearances&nbsp;
in "The Whole Nine Yards, "Planet of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:44.560
Apes," and "Daredevil," but none of those&nbsp;
films achieved the same level of attention.

00:03:44.560 --> 00:03:47.840
His performances in "Sin City"&nbsp;
and "The Island" were praised,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:47.840 --> 00:03:50.960
but outside of some voice work&nbsp;
and appearances in minor hits,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:50.960 --> 00:03:55.040
Duncan's body of work began to decline.&nbsp;
He worked throughout the early 2000s,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:55.040 --> 00:03:59.600
but achieving the same level of recognition he&nbsp;
earned for "The Green Mile" proved insurmountable.

00:03:59.600 --> 00:04:04.320
Duncan's acting career wasn't on a lot&nbsp;
of peoples' minds when he died in 2012,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:07.920
and it didn't help that his&nbsp;
posthumous releases were all duds.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:07.920 --> 00:04:12.521
If his profile had been higher, his death&nbsp;
would assuredly have been bigger news.

00:04:12.521 --> 00:04:16.880
Fans of Michael Clarke Duncan continue to&nbsp;
show surprise upon learning of his passing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:16.880 --> 00:04:18.800
On the Looper video about his death,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:18.800 --> 00:04:22.800
there are countless comments from fans&nbsp;
indicating they had no idea he died.

00:04:22.800 --> 00:04:25.280
One commenter said in 2017:

00:04:25.280 --> 00:04:28.800
"Michael Clark[e] Duncan has to be the&nbsp;
best supporting actor I've ever seen.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:28.800 --> 00:04:32.480
I wondered where he went. He would&nbsp;
have made a great X-Man character."

00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:34.560
Another person commented in 2020,

00:04:34.560 --> 00:04:37.600
"Michael Clarke Duncan [IS]&nbsp;
ONE OF MY FAVORITE ACTORS.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:37.600 --> 00:04:41.440
I ADORED THIS MAN TO NO END, AND&nbsp;
I NEVER REALIZED HE WAS DEAD."

00:04:41.440 --> 00:04:43.440
A 2019 comment said,

00:04:43.440 --> 00:04:46.000
"Michael Clarke Duncan was&nbsp;
one of my favorite actors!&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:46.000 --> 00:04:49.040
I love him so much! [...] I&nbsp;
just finally found out he died."

00:04:49.040 --> 00:04:52.800
That's just a tiny sampling of the&nbsp;
comments expressing sadness and shock&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:52.800 --> 00:04:56.960
fans felt upon learning of Duncan's death&nbsp;
years later. The video continues to receive&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:56.960 --> 00:05:01.360
comments like these every week. In&nbsp;
April 2022, one commenter wrote,

00:05:01.360 --> 00:05:06.480
"Oh my, I love Michael Duncan not knowing he's&nbsp;
dead already... May his soul rest in peace."

00:05:06.480 --> 00:05:10.948
Given the outpouring of love for Duncan, it's&nbsp;
likely comments like these will continue.

